<p>French voters cast first-round ballots in municipal elections across about 35,000 towns, villages, and cities on March 15. The results are being watched closely for clues about alliances and political momentum ahead of the 2027 presidential election, when President Emmanuel Macron cannot seek another term. While the races focused on local issues such as housing, security, and refuse collection, national parties treated them as an important test of organizational strength and local footholds before the next presidential campaign. Early results showed gains for Marine Le Pen&#x27;s National Rally in parts of the southeast, including a strong showing in Marseille, while Jean-Luc Mélenchon&#x27;s France Unbowed expanded its presence in several cities. Socialists also stayed competitive in places including Paris and Montpellier. That picture was tempered by unusually low turnout: abstention was estimated at between 41.5% and 44%, one of the highest levels for a municipal first round outside the pandemic-disrupted 2020 vote. Many contests now head to a runoff on March 22, where alliances and vote transfers could still reshape local outcomes.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/J2plelDWCnDY5Yk2Kl91i39c4OejkSq4rr8EtNjP4dUZOA2ibeSYEkz6MM_ubeOctIZH9R57QVePl-h2BhIPcs8Oiih_e-Njo8zJjzKiJGpcq05-GEMsQawGW0PK_pNxdp8rR5y0m8bMGqlVkMtXcvHL3zMjwvBvsTW4LNcjqZWr-32yHhAUXKj0YZMhwnyvlKvFlCQs3eEriA-moM9X7fkgKeg' alt='Supporters of Benoît Payan, the incumbent mayor of Marseille, distributing leaflets in the city on Friday. Mr. Payan is competing in a tight race featuring a strong far-right candidate.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Marseille test: In Marseille, incumbent mayor Benoît Payan faced a tight contest in France&#x27;s second city, where The New York Times described the strong far-right challenge as a bellwether for broader national shifts.</li><li>Toulouse surprise: France Unbowed highlighted François Piquemal&#x27;s 27.56% in Toulouse, where he edged Socialist François Briançon&#x27;s 24.99%, as evidence that the movement can finish first on the left beyond its best-known strongholds.</li><li>RN limits: Le Monde reported that despite significant gains in southeastern cities, the far right&#x27;s second-round prospects looked less favorable than first hoped because runoff dynamics and local alliances may limit how many mayoralties it can actually win.</li><li>Urban bastions: Socialist leads in Paris and Montpellier showed that the party still holds important city strongholds, even as France Unbowed gained ground elsewhere on the left.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>National Rally: The party framed the first round as a test of whether national popularity can turn into something more durable: local candidate lists, activists, and enough dealmaking capacity to win city halls. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/bd55b37f-f92f-4c56-b704-74feae9e9b99'>Financial Times</a>)</li><li>France Unbowed: The movement pointed to a targeted municipal strategy — prioritizing Roubaix, building a broader ticket in Saint-Denis, and overtaking the Socialists in Toulouse — as proof that it can compete to lead the left locally. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/municipales-tout-ce-quon-vous-conseille-de-retenir/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>Socialist Party: By staying ahead in several important cities, the Socialists kept leverage in runoff bargaining. They still have to decide where cooperation with France Unbowed strengthens them and where it blurs their identity. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/politics/article/2026/03/16/2026-municipal-election-results-key-takeaways-from-a-first-round-marked-by-low-turnout_6751474_5.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>French voters: Abstention on this scale left many local frontrunners backed by only a small share of registered voters, making the runoff crucial for anyone seeking a clearer local mandate. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/politics/article/2026/03/16/2026-french-municipal-elections-voter-abstention-reaches-levels-unprecedented-except-during-the-pandemic_6751482_5.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/french-voters-head-to-polls-in-first-round-of-municipal-elections-before-2027-presidential-race'>French voters head to polls in first round of municipal elections before 2027 presidential race</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/15/world/europe/france-marseille-mayor-election-far-right.html'>Marseille’s Tight Mayoral Race Is a Bellwether for France’s Future</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/15/french-local-elections-first-round-results'>First-round of French local elections sees strong showing for National Rally and LFI</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/municipales-tout-ce-quon-vous-conseille-de-retenir/'>Municipales : tout ce qu’on vous conseille de retenir</a> - politico.eu</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/bd55b37f-f92f-4c56-b704-74feae9e9b99'>French far-right makes first-round gains in municipal elections</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/politics/article/2026/03/16/2026-municipal-election-results-key-takeaways-from-a-first-round-marked-by-low-turnout_6751474_5.html'>2026 municipal election results: Key takeaways from a first round marked by low turnout</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.reutersconnect.com/item/the-first-round-of-municipal-elections-in-france/dGFnOnJldXRlcnMuY29tLDIwMjY6bmV3c21sX1JDMjE1S0ExUEhHVQ'>The first round of municipal elections is taking place in France.</a> - reutersconnect.com</li></ul>